 shooting because once you get noticed  you're gonna have to escape right you  have to get out you have to plan your  next move ahead because this is all one  continuous story right yes one  continuous story that focuses on this  guy named John north and he's going back  modern-day Georgia to find his brother  who's been taken by some kind of  separatist movement maybe brainwash  that's one of the central questions it's  not like one map though there's like  three maps so there is a story  progression and you can go back and  forth like shadow of mordor style  between the maps is more like early  Metal Gear Solid games where if you are  discovered you're kind of screwed or  that you kind of are hinting it maybe  you do have a fighting chance once  you're discovered I mean you have any  other side arms you can use or just like  you know equipment that'll help you  escape you do have a suppressed pistol  and you do have suppressed assault  rifles  however the suppressors are designed to  break after a couple of rounds right so  the game clearly wants you to go loud  just to escape and it does have some of  those elements from Far Cry such as when  you're escaping their outpost that you  can run into if you haven't cleared  earlier that could get you in a lot of  trouble and also the bases can start  firing mortar rounds if you really aggro  it so you can basically get bombed out  of existence so the game definitely  pushes you into the stealth route we  have a drone just scout the area and  figure out who to take out when almost  like a puzzle  sniping game at times right and then you  kill out only if you have to to get out  what does the actual sniping feel like  from your demo does it feel good was it  difficult like I imagine that would be  if they're really going for like  hardcore realism so the difficulty level  I played on had a moderate level of  realism mostly dealing with range in  windage if you dial in the range wrong  then your windage is off and you have a  good chance of missing your target  there's also some other things they take  into account how far away from your  target are when it comes to sounds so  you can actually use an unsuppressed  sniper rifle if you're more than I think  the Deaf side like 150 like yards away  they might not hear the shot and also  the game takes into account shadow like  real-time shadows so there's different  times a day if you're hiding shadows and  making your shots you might not get  spotted as opposed to just standing in  broad daylight  so yeah the the level of sniping it's  not hardcore like I wish games like this  would go a little bit more into helping  me way back when the Xbox one got  introduced they showed us the capability  the  box one controllers to figure out the  sensitivity of how hard you're pulling  the trigger and like also it is for  rumble motors and I kind of wish these  hardcore sniping games go a little bit  more into you actually having to make  the steady pull on the trigger or the  shot goes off and maybe like every gun  kicks a little differently though have  we have yet to see that in a sniping  game I do want to touch a little more on  the overall structure and gameplay loop  of the game you mentioned there's like a  economy and crafting system is that so  you're going to be doing missions and  maybe taking out certain targets and  then is that feeding back into going to  the safe houses and upgrading your  weapons or can you did you see much that  during the demo yeah they're  collectibles throughout the world  they're mostly Peas question marks all  over the map and then as you go through  the missions you find crates and there's  a currency system in a crafting system  because it's a persistent world I'm  assuming I don't know 100% but I'm  assuming you could probably just run out  of useful bullets at a certain point so  you have to always be going back to your  base and making these bullets they also  said there's a couple of friendly towns  so I'm assuming there's a trading system  at play there so it sounds like you'll  be doing activities to make sure your  gear is proper and up to speed in  between other missions in the game  cool thanks so much Aaron that is sniper  ghost Warrior 3 that will release on  April 4th 2017 for PC Xbox one and ps4  we will be hearing more news in the  coming months about the multiplayer  aspects of the game so for that stay  tuned to games.com  Oh

